---
title: "How Cloudflare Access learns GitHub org membership"
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: How Cloudflare Access learns GitHub org membership
  accDescr: Visitor hits Access. With no session, Access sends them to GitHub OAuth. GitHub returns a token. Access lists the user's orgs and matches the Allow policy. Allow sets a JWT cookie and the static HTML is served. Deny never reaches the origin.
  participant V as Visitor
  participant A as Cloudflare Access
  participant G as GitHub
  participant O as Static origin
  V->>A: GET team.docs - no JWT
  A-->>V: Access login
  V->>G: OAuth - orgs, teams, email
  G-->>A: short-lived token
  A->>G: GET /user/orgs
  G-->>A: [your-org, ...]
  alt org matches Allow policy
    A-->>V: set Access JWT cookie
    V->>O: GET with cookie
    O-->>V: static HTML and search index
  else not in org or app cannot see org
    A-->>V: deny - origin never runs
  end
